00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.430
Junius Seven has accelerated by two more percent.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:51.150
<b>Scars That Won't Heal</b>

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:51.150
<b>Scars That Won't Heal</b>

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:53.040
It remains on a collision course with Earth, zero, zero, five.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.000
What in the world happened?

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.360
Considering its mass, it's unthinkable that it could change course so easily.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.410
Have you contacted the Chairman on board the Minerva?

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.320
Are they sure it's headed for Earth?

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.020
What can we do to avoid a collision?

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.290
What about warning Earth?

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.010
What is it?

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:17.890
<i>Captain</i>.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:21.180
<i>The Supreme Council is on line number one. They want Chairman Durandal</i>.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:34.500
What?! Junius Seven is moving?

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:36.010
But how?!

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:38.390
I have no idea.

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:42.950
Only that it is in fact moving, and fast.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.160
It has taken the worst possible trajectory.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:48.700
We've been able to confirm the same with our own crew.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.040
But how could this ever happen?

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:55.780
It was said to be in a stable orbit, safe for hundreds of years.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.940
Either a collision with a meteor, or some other factor.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:05.050
The bottom line is, it's moving even as we speak...

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:06.850
It's headed for Earth.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:08.780
If it falls...

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:13.940
If it falls, what'll happen to Orb? Or to Earth for that matter?!

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.270
Considering its mass,

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:20.900
I'm sure you already have a good idea without me telling you.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:26.130
The PLANTs are doing everything they can to find out how this happened

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.170
and how to avoid a collision.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:33.010
I must apologize for involving you in yet another incident,

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:40.590
but I have ordered the Minerva to proceed {merged}toward Junius Seven as soon as repairs are finished.

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:43.880
Fortunately, we happen to be in close proximity.

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:47.760
I hope for your understanding, Princess.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:54.000
Of course! This is as grave a concern to us... as it is to you.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:58.050
If.. If there's anything at all that I can do to help...

00:04:58.480 --> 00:04:59.990
I understand how you feel.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.240
Right now, however, I ask that you please remain calm, Princess.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.780
If there's anything you can do, we'll be sure to let you know.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:13.830
It may be difficult, but we will try to establish direct contact with your nation.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:18.160
We will also take steps to have a ship come and pick you up as soon as possible.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.030
I see. Thank you.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.180
Yeah? But how could it have moved?

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:31.850
Either a meteoroid hit, or some other thing altered its orbit.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:35.330
Is it really on a collision course with Earth?

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.300
That's what Bart said.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.480
First, the robbery at Armory One, then before the dust even settles, this?

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:47.400
What's going on?

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.450
But what should we do?

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.610
Now then. What should we do with Junius Seven?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.380
Smash it to pieces.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.930
Smash it?

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:07.790
The whole thing?

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:12.930
It's impossible to change its orbit.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:17.330
If we want to avoid a collision, we have no choice but to smash it to pieces.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.980
But that thing's huge.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:24.530
It's at least 8 kilometers in diameter right through the middle!

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.940
How do we smash something that big?

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:31.700
And many of the bodies of those who died are still there.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.980
But if it drops, Earth will be annihilated.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:41.000
After that, nothing will remain. Not even those living on Earth now.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:45.760
Earth... destroyed?

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:47.410
That's right.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:48.930
That's terrible.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:55.560
But, well, I guess that's just how it is.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:57.850
It's beyond our control.

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:01.980
But it might end up being easier for us on the PLANTs,

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:05.890
since it takes care of a lot of stuff that way.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.870
How can you guys talk that way?!

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:14.030
"That's just how it is?!" "End up being easier?!"

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.590
Do you have any idea how serious this is?! What could happen to Earth?!

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:22.660
How many people will die as a result?! Do you guys realize what you're saying?!

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:25.540
I'm sorry...

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:30.540
So is that the way you people from ZAFT think?!

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:35.850
We went through that war! And we all suffered!

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.900
And finally, under Chairman Durandal's administration,

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:40.600
things seemed to be changing! Is that not the case?!

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:42.530
Stop it, Cagalli!

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:47.600
It's not as if Yolant really meant what he said.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:52.120
Can't you even tell the difference?!

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:53.320
How dare you?!

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.170
Cagalli!

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:56.450
Shinn, watch what you say.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:01.870
Oh, that's right. She's kind of a big deal, isn't she?

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:04.090
She's Orb's Representative, after all.

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:05.440
You...

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:07.230
Put a lid on it, Cagalli!

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:16.300
I take it you dislike Orb. May I ask why?

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.310
I hear you used to live there.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:26.110
Please refrain form picking a fight with the Representative over an unrelated, trivial reason.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:31.150
Trivial? I won't allow anyone to call it "trivial!"

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.240
And unrelated?! You're wrong on that account as well!

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:38.330
My family was killed because of the Athhas!

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:43.500
We believed in the nation, and we believed in your so-called ideals.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.170
And in the end, my family was killed at Onogoro!

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.300
That's why I will never believe you!

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:54.470
And I will never believe the nation of Orb!

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:57.600
I'll never believe any of your idealism again!

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.070
When you said you'd protect the nation's justice,

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:11.070
did you ever stop to think how many lives would be lost because of your actions?!

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:24.570
You don't have a clue. Stop talking like you know everything!

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:30.790
Hey! Shinn!

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:51.940
Now... this is just terrible.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:57.210
An unprecedented danger. A scenario for the Earth's destruction.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.950
Has anyone actually written one like this?

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:06.790
I've ordered Phantom Pain to return and investigate it. Just in case.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.530
Will things be all right?

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:09.990
Things will be fine.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:15.170
What good will an investigation do at this point?

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:17.250
That's what we're investigating.

00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:21.600
So, why are we meeting, Djibril?

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:30.060
Well, I can't imagine the Atlantic Federation and governments around the world sitting back and letting that thing fall.{merged}

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:33.870
They're all busy preparing evacuation plans should the thing indeed fall.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:42.090
To be honest, I'm shocked about what has happened.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:46.990
Junius Seven? How could it be? Why in the world?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.820
At first, that's all I could think about.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.580
Forget the prelude, Djibril.

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:57.430
No, this is precisely the point.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:03.380
Given the situation, eventually the whole world will be asking those same questions.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:08.680
Then we must provide them with answers.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:16.980
Durandal of the PLANTs has already issued a warning to all Earth nations

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:21.730
and sent the message that he is doing everything within his power to avoid a collision and deal with the situation.{merged}

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:24.160
He was very quick to do so.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.080
They're panicking as well.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:30.660
Then perhaps this really was caused naturally.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.500
But, if so...

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:36.300
No. None of that is important any longer.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:37.410
Oh?

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:40.290
What's important is what happens after this disaster.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.280
When the people search for answers as they weep,

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:46.890
the answers we provide them will be important.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:50.350
My, my. You're already thinking that far ahead.

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.740
Of course. Regardless of what caused it,

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:57.290
it's a fact that one clumsy, stupid object{merged}

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:00.940
is going to fall to Earth very soon.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:08.240
Think about it! Because of that thing, we end up looking like spineless fools

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:11.490
as we run around trying to find a way out of the mess!

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:18.230
Somebody must pay for this humiliation.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:25.200
But who?! Why, who other than the Coordinators who built that thing in the first place.{merged}

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:26.810
Am I wrong?

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:31.620
That's fine with me, but...

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:36.040
But depending on the casualties incurred,

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.860
we may no longer have the strength to fight a war.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:42.280
That's why I have gathered you here today.

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:46.970
Taking shelter and escaping are fine for now,

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:51.620
but immediately after that, we will launch our assault. With the plan.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:55.790
I wanted you all to understand this beforehand.

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.730
I see.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:00.380
You think aggressively.

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:05.720
With a growing hatred for the Coordinators, the people will be fired up. {merged}

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:07.740
If there are any left, that is.

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:12.030
We'll be uniting them, I imagine. With a love called "hatred".

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:18.230
It appears that everyone approves of the plan, Djibril.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.840
Thank you very much.

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:25.880
Then we shall meet next after the incident. Have a detailed plan prepared by then.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:26.580
Right.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:31.130
But I wonder how great the casualties will be.

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:34.640
Wars are fine, but these things are nothing but trouble.

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:38.540
Whatever the case, it's all for the preservation of our blue and pure world!

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:54.230
The Voltaire and the Rousseau have taken the Meteor Breakers and gone ahead.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.250
Right. We should hurry as well.

00:13:56.980 --> 00:13:59.790
Have the Earth Alliance Forces taken any action yet?

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:04.250
We have yet to receive word on any action taken by them.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:08.250
But they won't get there in time anyway, even if they do send over vessels from the Moon.{merged}

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:12.700
The best they can do now is fire missiles from Earth's surface to destroy it.

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:18.300
But that'll likely have little effect. It won't do much more than scorch the surface.

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:23.210
In any case, Earth is also our motherland.

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:27.880
We must do everything we can to deal with this unprecedented danger.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:32.240
What we can do with this ship and what it's equipped with might be limited,

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.570
but I ask that each and every one of you give it your all.

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:35.170
Yes, sir!

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:42.820
Cagalli...

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.850
There's no use thinking about it, Cagalli.

00:14:56.550 --> 00:15:00.630
You knew very well that there would be people like that.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.250
But...

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.720
For him to talk of my father in that way!

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:26.200
My father suffered a great deal over the decisions he made.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:27.640
Yet he...

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:31.580
But there's nothing we can do about it.

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:34.350
Asking him to try and understand won't help.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.950
Right now, there's no way he could understand.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:41.000
I'm sure his own feelings are already overwhelming enough.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:48.300
You do realize that, don't you, Cagalli?

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.560
Looking at it again, this thing is really huge.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:08.230
Of course it is! We live on one just like it, you know!

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:14.660
No, I'm talking about the extent of our next mission.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:18.730
Listen! This is a time-sensitive operation!

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:21.590
The Minerva's also on its way. Work effectively!

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:22.590
Roger!

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:25.770
<i>Confirming dodeca-pralimate charges loaded</i>.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:29.980
<i>Ignition on breakers one through four to be set to 215</i>.

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:33.340
<i>All others, set to 738</i>.

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:54.570
Huh? Is the Princess feeling better?

00:16:56.190 --> 00:17:01.390
She also lost her father and friends in that war.

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:05.120
It's not as if she doesn't have a clue.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:19.100
What is it?

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.290
No. Nothing.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.390
Don't worry about it. I'm not upset.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:28.190
What you said was correct.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:32.030
1200 to Junius Seven.

00:17:32.310 --> 00:17:33.820
Bringing up an optical image.

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:37.560
Can you open a line to the Voltaire?

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:40.030
No, we can't get a normal line yet!

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:44.250
What's the matter, Athrun? Oh, Alex, was it?

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:48.370
I ask you this, knowing it would be unconventional.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:51.700
Please lend me one of your mobile suits!

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:01.890
That certainly would be very difficult to do.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:07.160
Do you seriously think I could authorize that, under the circumstances?

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:11.690
Do you want to put former Chairman Canaver's efforts to waste?

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:17.280
I understand completely. But given the situation, I can't just watch and do nothing.

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:20.320
If you do have a machine that's usable, then please!

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:24.890
I know how you feel, but...

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:27.210
Very well. I'll authorize it.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.600
This is under my jurisdiction, as Chairman.

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:30.380
Chairman?!

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.580
However, Chairman...

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.740
This is not a battle situation, Captain.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:44.390
The more machines we can get out there, the better.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:48.120
And you're well aware of his great skills.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:54.930
What?!

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:57.860
What in the world?!

00:18:58.740 --> 00:18:59.530
GINNs?! {}

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:02.160
What's going on?! Who do they belong to?!

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:05.200
Unknown! No response from the IFF!

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:06.470
What?!

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:13.590
How would you explain there being ZAFT mobile suits at the site?

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:20.680
Beats me. Perhaps this disturbance isn't a whimsical act of God, after all.

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:25.360
Send out Sting and the others. I want a better grasp of the situation.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:27.850
Give me as much info about this as possible.

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:33.020
<i>Three minutes to mobile suit launch. All pilots are to standby aboard your machines</i>.

00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:38.130
<i>I repeat. Three minutes to take off. All pilots are to standby aboard your machines</i>.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.960
We're supposed to help smash it apart, but what are we expected to do?

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:40.930
Well...

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.570
That guy's flying out as well, I'm told.

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:48.110
They say for support work like this, the more machines we can get out, the better.

00:19:48.110 --> 00:19:52.210
Really. Well, he is a mobile suit pilot, after all.

00:19:53.150 --> 00:19:53.880
He is?

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:56.210
One minute to mobile suit launch.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:20:00.050
Tell them to follow the orders of Commander Joule once they get there.

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:03.390
Detecting heat emissions indicating a battle at Junius Seven!

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:05.050
They're mobile suits!

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:06.360
<i>Abort launch!</i>

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:07.560
<i>The situation has changed</i>.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:10.770
<i>The Joule Team is engaged with an unknown opponent at Junius Seven</i>.

00:20:11.870 --> 00:20:12.730
Yzak?

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:13.900
Unknown?

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:18.230
<i>All units, alter your equipment for anti-mobile suit combat</i>.

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:21.900
Bogey One also confirmed! Green 25, Delta!

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:22.900
That's here?!

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:27.150
What's going on?!

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:28.080
<i>I have no idea</i>.

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:32.770
<i>What remains unchanged is that our mission is to support the Joule Team!</i>

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:35.790
<i>Upon completing equipment switch, please proceed for take off!</i>

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:46.380
<i>Central catapult online</i>.

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:50.300
<i>Launch area commencing depressurization sequence</i>.

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:55.870
<i>Emergency crew, standby</i>. <i>Core Splendor, all systems online</i>.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:58.010
<i>Commencing takeoff sequence</i>.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:00.020
Even Bogey One's here.

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:11.290
<i>The situation has changed</i>. <i>It could be dangerous</i>.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:14.370
<i>Would you rather not go?</i>

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:16.670
Give me a little respect!

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:22.630
Shinn Asuka, Core Splendor, taking off!

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:52.080
Rey Za Burrel, ZAKU, taking off!

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:59.500
<b>tooku hanareteru hodo ni chikaku ni kanjiteru</b>

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:59.500
<b>The further we are apart, the nearer I feel you are</b>

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:59.880
Lunamaria Hawke, ZAKU, taking off!

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:10.180
<b>samishisa mo tsuyosa eto kawatteku... kimi wo omottanara</b>

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:10.180
<b>Even my loneliness turns into strength... when I think of you</b>

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:11.850
Course is clear. Please take off!

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:14.020
Athrun Zala, taking off!

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:25.690
<b>kotoba wo kasanete mo wakari aenai koto</b>

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:25.690
I still did not realize

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:32.490
<b>
mada shiranakatta ne</b>

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:32.490
That there are things that can't be conveyed even with words

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:40.130
<b>kimi dake wo dakishimetakute nakushita yume kimi wa</b>

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:40.130
My lost dreams of wanting to hold you by my side,

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:47.090
<b>
"akiramenaide" to itta</b>

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:47.090
For them, you said, "Don't give up!"

00:22:46.380 --> 00:22:53.930
<b>tooku hanareteru hodo ni chikaku ni kanjiteru</b>

00:22:46.380 --> 00:22:53.930
The further we are apart, the nearer I feel you are

00:22:53.220 --> 00:23:02.060
<b>
samishisa mo tsuyosa eto kawatteku... kimi wo omottanara</b>

00:22:53.220 --> 00:23:02.060
Even my loneliness turns into strength... when I think of you

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:08.780
<b>setsunaku mune wo sasu sore wa yume no kakera</b>

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:08.780
The thing that pierces the gentle chest, that's a fragment of my dream

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:21.750
<b>
arinomama deaeteta sono kiseki mou ichido shinjite</b>

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:21.750
Believe once more in the the miracle that is our chanced meeting

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:23.880
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:23.880
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:29.510
The scars of sorrow and pain always remain unseen within the heart.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:35.000
Are tragedies repeated because people can't see the depth of each other's scars?

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:38.930
What does everyone desire from deep within the heart? {}

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:43.770
Next, on Mobile Suit Gundam Seed Destiny,

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:45.900
"The End of the World."

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>The End of the World</b>

00:23:45.900 --> 00:23:51.950
<b>The End of the World</b>

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:49.320
Dash through the pitch black skies, Gaia!
